Q: How can I get my table to sort columns and keep the rows intact in egui? A: <pre><code>The root cause isn’t the table — it’s state synchronization between sorted data and actions.

Right now, you:

Sort filtered_waypoints

But perform actions on self.waypoints using a mismatched index

A cleaner and more robust pattern is to store indices alongside your filtered data before sorting. 
let mut filtered_waypoints: Vec&lt;(usize, &amp;Waypoint)&gt; = self.waypoints
    .iter()
    .enumerate()
    .collect();

// Apply sorting on tuple
filtered_waypoints.sort_by(|a, b| {
    let (idx_a, wa) = a;
    let (idx_b, wb) = b;

    let cmp = wa.name.cmp(&amp;wb.name); // example

    if self.sort_ascending {
        cmp
    } else {
        cmp.reverse()
    }
});
</code></pre>

